---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
const updated = '2026-10-11';
---

<Base title="Terms of Service" description={`Terms of Service for ${SITE.name} and its data API.`} path="/terms">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <p>
        These Terms govern your use of {SITE.name} (the “Service”), operated by {SITE.operator}, including
        the website, the news feed, and the data API. By accessing the Service you agree to these Terms. If
        you do not agree, do not use the Service.
      </p>

      <h2>1. The Service</h2>
      <p>
        The Service publishes original market briefs written from data we collect ourselves, attributed news
        digests that link their source, market and price snapshots, deterministic daily direction signals
        (<code>Rising</code>/<code>Falling</code>/<code>Steady</code>/<code>Choppy</code>), and a REST API.
        All data is provided for informational purposes only.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Not financial advice</h2>
      <p>
        The Service does <strong>not</strong> provide financial, investment, legal, or tax advice. Signals,
        prices, news, and any other output are informational only and must not be relied upon as a
        recommendation to buy, sell, or hold any asset. You are solely responsible for your decisions and
        for consulting a qualified professional where appropriate.
      </p>

      <h2>3. API keys and acceptable use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You must display “Powered by {SITE.name}” attribution, linked to {SITE.domain}.</li>
        <li>You may not resell, redistribute, or commercialize the data without a written agreement.</li>
        <li>You must respect documented rate limits and quotas; abuse may result in suspension or revocation.</li>
        <li>Keys are per-project, non-transferable, and stored only as hashes; keep your key secure.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranties of any kind. Data may be
        delayed, incomplete, or inaccurate. There is no SLA. We may change limits, endpoints, and data
        coverage at any time without notice.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, {SITE.operator} is not liable for any indirect, incidental,
        consequential, or special damages, or for any trading losses, arising from your use of the Service.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Third-party content</h2>
      <p>
        News items are derived from third-party sources and republished with attribution. Rights in the
        underlying reporting remain with those sources. If you believe content infringes your rights,
        contact us and we will address it promptly.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update these Terms; material changes will be reflected by the “last updated” date above.</p>

      <h2>8. Contact</h2>
      <p><a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
